- What metrics would indicate token misuse?

## Why This Question Is Asked
This evaluates practical controls for vendor-integrated cloud data access and cross-service trust boundaries.

## Key Concepts
- PKCE and short-lived tokens prevent token replay and limit exposure windows
- Token binding and mTLS establish bidirectional trust between services
- Dynamic credential rotation minimizes the blast radius of leaked secrets
- Policy-as-code IAM checks enable automated, repeatable security enforcement
- Incident response playbooks ensure rapid containment and recovery

## Code Example
```javascript
const verifyPKCE = (codeChallenge, codeVerifier, method = 'S256') => {
  if (method === 'S256') {
    const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256')
      .update(codeVerifier)
      .digest('base64url');
    return hash === codeChallenge;
  }
  return codeVerifier === codeChallenge;
};

const validateTokenBinding = (token, clientCert, deviceFingerprint) => {
  return token.binding.certThumbprint === clientCert.thumbprint
    && token.binding.deviceId === deviceFingerprint.id;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about cross-tenant data isolation, token binding, and incident response in a realistic multi-tenant platform similar to large-scale chat/workspace products.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege per-automation scopes
- Token binding to tenant identity and audience (aud/iss)
- Short-lived tokens with rapid rotation
- Per-resource RBAC/ACL enforcement
- API gateway policy checks and runtime validation
- Tamper-evident audit logs and a 24h IR playbook

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation: verify JWT claims for a request
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authorize(token, requiredScope, tenantId) {
  const payload = jwt.verify(token, PUBLIC_KEY, { algorithms:['RS256'] });
  if (payload.aud !== 'automation') return false;
  if (payload.tenant !== tenantId) return false;
  if (!payload.scopes.includes(requiredScope)) return false;
  // ensure token is recent
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design token rotation and revocation in case of breach?
- What telemetry would you collect to detect automation token abuse?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests data governance and cloud IAM proficiency in regulated fintech environments, focusing on data lake isolation and rapid IR.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with tenant attributes
- Deny-by-default bucket policies
- Data-centric protection (field-level encryption/tokenization)
- Policy drift detection (IAM Access Analyzer, CloudTrail)
- Incident response for data leakage (IR playbook, forensics)

## Code Example
